// Kagi Search REST (kagi.com/api/v1): the `kagi` provider of the web_search
// chain.
//
// Search only. Kagi's Universal Summarizer and FastGPT are answer endpoints
// and are not declared; neither is the Extract API. The Search API is a keyed
// search endpoint that returns result links, so this provider is built.
//
// Wire contract pinned from Kagi's own documentation (read 2026-10-20):
// - the published OpenAPI 3.0 document behind https://kagi.com/api/docs,
//   https://redocly-api-docs.kagi.com/api/docs/_bundle/openapi.yaml (server,
//   the `search` operation, its request schema, responses and the `kagi`
//   security scheme), rendered at
//   https://kagi.com/api/docs/openapi/search/search;
// - the API Quick Start and Search API pages,
//   https://help.kagi.com/kagi/api/api-portal.html and
//   https://help.kagi.com/kagi/api/search.html;
// - the search operators page,
//   https://help.kagi.com/kagi/features/search-operators.html.
//
// - method and path: POST https://kagi.com/api/v1/search (OpenAPI server
//   https://kagi.com/api/v1, operation POST /search) with a JSON body. The
//   transport URL is the host and the path carries /api/v1/search;
// - auth: the OpenAPI `kagi` security scheme is `type: http, scheme: bearer`
//   ("Kagi API key from https://kagi.com/api/keys"), so the key goes in
//   `Authorization` with the `Bearer ` prefix. The connection is bound to the
//   vault credential `apikey:kagi`; plexus reads it by name at dispatch and
//   never stores it;
// - request fields used: `query` (required; no maximum length documented),
//   `workflow` (default `search`; sent as the reviewed constant "search" so
//   the reply is web results, never images, videos, news or podcasts),
//   `limit` (documented 1 to 1024; it "only limits the maximum amount
//   returned"), `lens.sites_included` ("Search only these domains") for
//   requested domains, and `filters.after` (format `date`, "results published
//   or updated after this date") for a recency window. The OpenAPI also
//   documents format, lens_id, the other lens options, timeout, page,
//   filters.region and filters.before, extract (billed extra), safe_search
//   (default true) and personalizations; none are sent and they are not in
//   the reviewed schema;
// - reply: {meta, data}. `data` holds result buckets of one shared item
//   schema (required `url` and `title`; optional `snippet`, `time`, `image`,
//   `props`). Only `data.search` ("all search results for html pages or
//   websites") is read: its `title`, `url`, `snippet` and `time` (an
//   RFC 3339 timestamp, "when the resource was created or last updated").
//   No bucket is required by the schema, so a `data` object without `search`
//   is an empty result. `data.direct_answer` (quick answers such as maths or
//   unit conversions), `data.infobox` and every other bucket are never read,
//   so no answer text reaches a caller;
// - errors (errorEnvelope: meta, data null or empty, error[] of code, url,
//   message, location): 400 invalid request parameters, 401 "Access token is
//   missing or invalid", 403 "Forbidden - IP address not authorized", 429
//   "Rate limited or usage limit exhausted" and 500. No 402 and no
//   Retry-After header are documented.
//
// Differences from the provider facts the web_search chain design started from
// (Kagi search API at kagi.com/api, search not summarizer; bearer; query and
// limit, with domains and dates as query syntax; search result items' title,
// url and snippet):
// - auth: the help pages' examples send "Authorization: Bot $TOKEN" (and a GET
//   with ?q=), which conflicts with the OpenAPI document. The OpenAPI bearer
//   scheme and its POST operation are followed here;
// - domains travel in the native `lens.sites_included` field, not as `site:`
//   operators in the query. The field is documented on this operation with no
//   plan restriction, and the OpenAPI says lens options take precedence over
//   operators in the search terms, so it cannot be widened by the caller's
//   own text. Kagi documents no limit on its length; the tool's 20 applies;
// - recency travels in the native `filters.after` as a UTC YYYY-MM-DD day,
//   not as query syntax: Kagi's operators page documents site:, grouping,
//   AND, OR, +, -, quotes and *, but no date operator, and an undocumented
//   `after:` could be ignored and return results of any age. Every recency
//   window (day, week, month, year) is supported;
// - `limit` is reviewed as 1 to 20, the tool's own maximum, not Kagi's 1024;
// - query length: none is documented, so the tool's own 500-character limit
//   applies and no valid tool query skips Kagi for capability;
// - a publication date is reported from `time` when it is a parseable date;
// - undeclared quota gap: Kagi's official OpenAPI bundle above (read
//   2026-10-20) defines 429 as both rate limited and usage limit exhausted,
//   but no stable quota-specific error[].code or response header. No signal
//   is declared: both retain throttling (Retry-After if sent, or 60 seconds).
//   401 remains a credential failure, 400 a rejected request, and 403 and 500
//   unavailable for 60 seconds;
// - the Search page notes that the API inherits the account's settings
//   (blocked or promoted sites, snippet length). Those can reorder or remove
//   results but are not part of this contract.
//
// The search action is read-risk and has no side effects, so a retry is safe.
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "key": "kagi_rest",
  "name": "Kagi Search (REST)",
  "description": "Web search over Kagi's Search API (kagi.com/api/v1), as a provider for web_search.",
  "reuse_path": "openapi_shim",
  "reuse_rationale": "Documented REST API with a published OpenAPI spec and static API-key bearer auth; a search mutates no vendor-side state, so it maps to a read grant.",
  "tier": "S1",
  "transport": {
    "kind": "rest_api",
    "url": "https://kagi.com"
  },
  "auth": {
    "mode": "api_key"
  },
  "credential_bindings": [
    {
      "ref_role": "api_key",
      "placement": "header",
      "key": "Authorization",
      "prefix": "Bearer ",
      "required": true
    }
  ],
  "resource_filters": {
    "required": [],
    "optional": [],
    "write_enabling": []
  },
  "actions_baseline": [
    {
      "name": "search",
      "risk": "read",
      "http": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/api/v1/search",
        "request_constants": {
          "workflow": "search"
        },
        "args_schema": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "query": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 500 },
            "limit": { "type": "integer", "minimum": 1, "maximum": 20 },
            "lens": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "sites_included": {
                  "type": "array",
                  "items": { "type": "string", "minLength": 1, "maxLength": 253 },
                  "minItems": 1,
                  "maxItems": 20
                }
              },
              "required": ["sites_included"],
              "additionalProperties": false
            },
            "filters": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "after": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "format": "date",
                  "pattern": "^[0-9]{4}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}$"
                }
              },
              "required": ["after"],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          },
          "required": ["query"],
          "additionalProperties": false
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "ask_first_risk": ["write", "destructive"]
  },
  "availability": "ga"
}
